      },
      {
        "angle": "The Symmetrical Counterfactual Appeal Reality",
        "argument": "Reinforce Colleagues 2, 7, 9, 13, 14, 16, 17, and 21: An exam board cannot key an arbitrary choice between F and F′. In an appeal, an examinee who wrote F′ would be identical to F. A key that depends on an arbitrary coin-flip between two identical paralogs is an invalid item key. The only objective key is H."
